  "issue_number": 3370,
  "issue_title": "Add reusable FreshnessBadge (\"as of / N ago\" + realtime-vs-daily tier) component",
  "issue_body": "## Context\nFreshness is currently rendered by two disconnected, partial primitives: `FreshnessIndicator` in `apps/ui/src/components/metagraphed/freshness.tsx` (dot + relative time only, via `formatRelative`/`isStaleFreshness` from `lib/metagraphed/format.ts`), used solely on `subnet-masthead.tsx`; and a separate `formatFreshness`/`formatFreshnessAbsolute` pair in `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/freshness.ts`, consumed by `methodology-callout.tsx`, `schema-drift-detail.tsx`, `operational-panel.tsx`, `stat-with-spark.tsx`, `spark-legend.tsx`, `uptime-timeline.tsx`, and `registry-empty.tsx` for absolute \"as of\" timestamps. Neither expresses a realtime-vs-daily **tier** concept, so five downstream issues (#3376, #3378, #3379, #3380, #3381) that need to label data as \"realtime block tier\" vs \"daily rollup tier\" have no shared component to build on and would otherwise each hand-roll their own badge markup.\n\n## Requirement\nAdd a single reusable `FreshnessBadge` component that renders both an \"as of \\<absolute time\\>\" and \"\\<N ago\\>\" relative phrasing plus an explicit realtime-vs-daily tier label/style, built on the existing `formatRelative`/`isStaleFreshness`/`formatFreshnessAbsolute` primitives rather than reimplementing time math \u2014 it does not need to replace every existing consumer in this PR, only exist and be exported so the five tier-labeling issues above can adopt it.\n\n## Deliverable\n- New file: `apps/ui/src/components/metagraphed/freshness-badge.tsx` (co-located with the existing `freshness.tsx`), exporting `FreshnessBadge`\n- Reuse, don't reimplement: import `formatRelative` + `isStaleFreshness` from `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/format.ts` and `formatFreshnessAbsolute` from `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/freshness.ts` \u2014 the same primitives `FreshnessIndicator` (`apps/ui/src/components/metagraphed/freshness.tsx:18`) and the `stat-with-spark.tsx`/`spark-legend.tsx` call sites already use\n- Props: `at?: string | null` (the timestamp), a new `tier: \"realtime\" | \"daily\"` (or equivalent literal union) driving a visible label/style distinction (\"Live\" vs \"Daily rollup\"-style wording), and pass-throughs for `thresholdMs`/`className` matching `FreshnessIndicator`'s existing `Props` shape (`freshness.tsx:4-11`) for drop-in familiarity\n- Render both time forms together: the absolute \"as of HH:MM\u2026\" string (`formatFreshnessAbsolute`) alongside the \"N ago\" relative string (`formatRelative`), plus the existing dot-color staleness cue (`bg-health-ok`/`bg-health-warn`/`bg-health-unknown`) from `FreshnessIndicator`\n- This PR adds the component only \u2014 it does not need to migrate `subnet-masthead.tsx`'s existing `FreshnessIndicator` usage (`subnet-masthead.tsx:294`) or any of the seven `lib/metagraphed/freshness.ts` consumers; those are separate follow-ups (#3376, #3378, #3379, #3380, #3381 each apply a tier to one specific page)\n- Coordination: this is explicitly the **foundational** item for the \"Live UX + freshness\" cluster in #2542 \u2014 #3371 (polling refresh hook) is a sibling foundation piece, not a dependency of this one; #3376/#3378/#3379/#3380/#3381 all consume `FreshnessBadge` once it exists\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] `apps/ui/src/components/metagraphed/freshness-badge.tsx` exists and exports `FreshnessBadge`\n- [ ] `FreshnessBadge` accepts an `at` timestamp prop and a `tier: \"realtime\" | \"daily\"` prop (or equivalently named literal union) that changes the rendered label/style\n- [ ] Component renders both an absolute \"as of\" string and a relative \"N ago\" string from the same `at` value\n- [ ] Implementation imports `formatRelative`/`isStaleFreshness` from `lib/metagraphed/format.ts` and `formatFreshnessAbsolute` from `lib/metagraphed/freshness.ts` rather than reimplementing relative-time or staleness math\n- [ ] A unit test file (e.g. `apps/ui/src/components/metagraphed/freshness-badge.test.tsx`) covers: realtime vs daily tier rendering, stale vs fresh dot state, and missing/null `at`\n- [ ] No existing consumer (`subnet-masthead.tsx`, `methodology-callout.tsx`, `schema-drift-detail.tsx`, `operational-panel.tsx`, `stat-with-spark.tsx`, `spark-legend.tsx`, `uptime-timeline.tsx`, `registry-empty.tsx`) is modified in this PR \u2014 it is additive only\n- [ ] Before/after screenshot table in the PR showing the new badge in isolation (e.g. a Storybook-style ad hoc render or a temporary mount point), per the repo's UI-change screenshot rule\n\n## Non-goals\n- Do not migrate `subnet-masthead.tsx`'s existing `FreshnessIndicator` call, or any of the seven `formatFreshness`/`formatFreshnessAbsolute` consumers, to the new `FreshnessBadge` \u2014 that's the job of #3376/#3378/#3379/#3380/#3381 and the other per-page freshness-label issues in #2542, done one page at a time\n- Do not build the polling/auto-refresh mechanism \u2014 that is #3371, a separate foundational piece\n- Do not delete or deprecate `FreshnessIndicator` (`components/metagraphed/freshness.tsx`) or the `lib/metagraphed/freshness.ts` formatters in this PR; consolidating/retiring the older primitives, if warranted, is a follow-up decision for after adoption, not part of this deliverable\n- No backend/API changes \u2014 this is presentation-only, consuming timestamps the API already returns\n\n## Size\nSize: S \u2014 keep this PR small (aim for \u226410 files / \u22641000 LOC).\n\nPart of #2542.",
